(ned MEASURE ALL TOOLS -- step 4, the last of the probing reset.)
(Operator 2026-08-11: "it assumes all tools are in the rack, and it picks)
(them up and touches them all off, one at a time".)

(IT DRIVES THE RACK. This is the only step in the chain that moves the)
(machine on its own for minutes at a time, once per tool, and it will run)
(the changer as many times as the rack has tools. Nothing here is a probe)
(trick: each pass is an ordinary M6 followed by PB's own tool_touch_off,)
(the same routine the single-tool button uses, so a tool measured by this)
(loop is measured exactly as it would have been by hand.)

(THE RACK MAP IS THE TRUTH, not the tool table. #[4000+fork] is what the)
(changer itself believes is sitting in each fork; a tool in the table but)
(not in a fork cannot be fetched, and asking for it would drive the head to)
(an empty pocket. So the loop walks forks, not tool numbers.)

(THE SPINDLE MUST START EMPTY. If something is clamped, the first M6 puts)
(it away -- which is fine -- but only if the rack has a home for it, and if)
(it does not the changer has nowhere to go mid-cycle. Refusing up front is)
(cheaper than discovering it with a tool in the air.)

(EVERY LENGTH IS WRITTEN BY tool_touch_off ITSELF. This file deliberately)
(does no arithmetic on lengths: one place computes them, and it is the one)
(that already worked.)
o<cal_measure_all> sub
  #<forks> = #1
  o1 if [#<forks> LE 0]
    (default = the live fork count in #3973, not a literal)
    #<forks> = #3973
    o99 if [#<forks> LT 1]
      #<forks> = 14
    o99 endif
  o1 endif
  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, MEASURE ALL: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o10 if [#3010 EQ 0]
    (abort, MEASURE ALL: no spindle nose height - run the calibration chain first)
  o10 endif
  o11 if [#3007 LE 0]
    (abort, MEASURE ALL: no plunge allowance - run SET PROBE HEIGHT first)
  o11 endif
  o12 if [#5183 EQ 0]
    (abort, MEASURE ALL: no probe height in G30 - run SET PROBE HEIGHT first)
  o12 endif
  o13 if [#5400 GT 0]
    (abort, MEASURE ALL: put the spindle tool away first - this cycle starts and ends empty)
  o13 endif

  #<n>    = 1
  #<done> = 0
  o20 while [#<n> LE #<forks>]
    #<t> = #[4000 + #<n>]
    o21 if [#<t> GT 0]
      (PRINT, MEASURE ALL: fork #<n> holds T#<t> - fetching it.)
      M6 T#<t>
      G43
      (guard the fetch: if the changer did not end up holding what the rack)
      (map promised, measuring would write the length onto the wrong tool)
      o22 if [#5400 NE #<t>]
        (abort, MEASURE ALL: asked for T#<t> but the spindle reports a different tool - stopping before a length is written to the wrong one)
      o22 endif
      o<tool_touch_off> call
      #<done> = [#<done> + 1]
      (PRINT, MEASURE ALL: T#<t> measured. #<done> so far.)
    o21 endif
    #<n> = [#<n> + 1]
  o20 endwhile

  (put the last one back so the cycle ends the way it started)
  o30 if [#5400 GT 0]
    M6 T0
  o30 endif
  (PRINT, MEASURE ALL DONE: #<done> tools measured and returned to the rack.)
  (DEBUG, MEASURE ALL DONE: #<done> tools)
o<cal_measure_all> endsub
M2 (end program)
